# novadeck — the earlyoom operator override file, deliberately EMPTY of defaults.
#
# This path belongs to the earlyoom package, which ships it containing an active
#
#   EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 -n --avoid '(^|/)(init|systemd|Xorg|sshd)$'"
#
# We overwrite it with this comments-only version. WHY: earlyoom.service expands $EARLYOOM_ARGS
# AFTER novadeck's own settings (see /usr/lib/systemd/system/earlyoom.service.d/novadeck.conf), and
# earlyoom parses with getopt, where the LAST occurrence of an option wins outright — a second
# --avoid REPLACES the first rather than adding to it. So the packaged defaults did not merge with
# our policy, they silently displaced the parts they overlapped.
#
# Measured on hardware before this file existed: the device logged
#   Will avoid killing process names that match regex '(^|/)(init|systemd|Xorg|sshd)$'
# i.e. the packaged list, not ours. Every name in our --avoid regex had no bias at all, and our
# -r 0 was overridden back to hourly reports. Only -M, -S and --ignore survived, because those
# happen to be the options the packaged file does not set.
#
# Emptying it is what makes the drop-in's design work as written, and it costs nothing: the packaged
# values were a generic desktop default (Xorg, which this image does not run) rather than anything
# tuned for this device.
#
# THIS FILE IS STILL THE OPERATOR SURFACE, and that is the point of emptying it rather than deleting
# it. Setting EARLYOOM_ARGS below overrides novadeck's policy — it is expanded last, so it wins on
# any option it names, and leaves the rest of the policy in place. That is the supported way to
# retune earlyoom on a device over SSH without editing /usr.
#
# Note for anyone doing that: an edit here lands in the /etc overlay's upper (which lives in /var)
# and therefore persists across updates, masking later versions of this file. If a future image
# changes the packaged defaults, a device that has been edited will not see the change.

# Options to pass to earlyoom. Unset by default — policy lives in
# /usr/lib/systemd/system/earlyoom.service.d/novadeck.conf.
#
# Examples:
#
# Memory report every minute (0 disables reports entirely, which is novadeck's default):
# EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 60"
#
# Act at 5% available memory instead of novadeck's absolute 400 MB threshold:
# EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 5"
#
# See `earlyoom -h` for the full option list.
